questions.a:
```sql
-- (a)
ALTER TABLE PRODUCT ADD Discount DECIMAL(5,2) DEFAULT 0.00;
-- (b)
ALTER TABLE PRODUCT MODIFY Price DECIMAL(10,2);
-- (c)
ALTER TABLE PRODUCT ADD CONSTRAINT chk_price_positive CHECK (Price > 0);
-- (d)
ALTER TABLE PRODUCT DROP COLUMN Category;
```
A wrong answer reveals: (a) forgetting DEFAULT clause, causing NULLs in existing rows; (b) using CHANGE instead of MODIFY (MySQL syntax confusion) or not realizing MODIFY can widen but not safely narrow if data exists; (c) writing CHECK inline without CONSTRAINT name (MySQL 8.0+ requires it) or putting it in wrong ALTER syntax; (d) not knowing DROP COLUMN syntax or that it removes data permanently.
